// The simplest thing the simulation does, predicted from the constants and
// then asserted. If this fails, nothing below it means anything.
//
// Motor acceleration 60m/s² adds 1m/s each tick after 10% drag.
// v(n)=10(1-.9^n) until capped at 9m/s on tick 22. Each tick's whole change
// (drag included) ramps in over four substeps, so a tick covers
// (v + 5/8 change) * dt. The first 30 displacements sum to 3.45787848m.
// Facing turns toward atan2(1, 0) = PI/2 at PLAYER_TURN_RATE 14 rad/s, which
// covers 1.5708 rad in 6.7 ticks — so by tick 30 it has arrived and clamped.
(
    description: "Walking accelerates to its target speed and covers the predicted distance while facing east.",
    setup: (),
    inputs: [
        (at: 0, ticks: 30, dir: (1.0, 0.0)),
    ],
    budget: (ticks: 30),
    expect: (
        player_pos: (x: 3.4578785, z: 0.0, tol: 0.001),
        facing: (value: 1.5708, tol: 0.0001),
        contacts: 0,
    ),
)
